# Optional first-start overrides for `docker compose up`.
#
# Copying this file to .env is optional: without it, the db service generates
# the database password and the JWT signing key on the first start.
# The values are read only on the first start, while the `secrets` volume
# holds no secrets; later starts ignore them. A change takes effect only after
# `docker compose down -v`, which resets the secrets and the database together.
# Never commit .env: it can hold secrets, and .gitignore excludes it.
#
# Leave a value blank to have it generated. A value you set must be a single
# line made only of the characters A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ ~ + / = -
#   SMARTHOTEL_DB_PASSWORD      16-128 characters
#   SMARTHOTEL_JWT_SIGNING_KEY  32-256 characters
# An invalid value stops the db service with an error naming the variable.
SMARTHOTEL_DB_PASSWORD=
SMARTHOTEL_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=
